# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore — BrownBearDielAct analysis pipeline
# ==============================================================================
# Keep the repository to source + the small synthetic example inputs only.
# Large binaries, container images, raw data and generated outputs stay out.

# ---- Container images (build from the Dockerfile instead) --------------------
*.sif
*.simg
*.img

# ---- R session / project cruft ----------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rapp.history
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# ---- Serialized R objects & intermediate outputs -----------------------------
# (regenerated by the pipeline; never committed)
*.rds
*.RDS

# ---- Large third-party climate rasters (download per data/README.md) ---------
*.nc
*.nc4

# ---- Pipeline output directories (created under the analysis root at runtime)-
logs/
checkpoints/
models/
figures/
tables/

# ---- Raw private inputs (kept out; ship only example_data/) -------------------
# The real Activity/, Position/ and Bear_metadata.xlsx live outside the repo.
# NOTE: raw-input folders you DO ship (EnvironmentalPreds/, shapefiles/,
# data/README.md) are committed — they are not matched by any rule above.

# ---- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- OS / editor junk --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# ==============================================================================
# Explicitly KEEP the shipped synthetic example inputs (they must be committed)
# ==============================================================================
!example_data/
!example_data/**
